## Corrected trajectory description (chronological order, 1100 -> 500 BCE)

| BCE (chronological) | PC1 score | diff score(1100)-score(bin) |
|----:|----:|----:|
| 1100 | 4.452 | - |
| 1000 | 2.172 | +2.280 |
| 900  | 1.654 | +2.798 |
| 800  | 1.910 | +2.542 |
| 700  | 1.247 | +3.205 |
| 600  | 0.829 | +3.623 |
| 500  | 0.815 | +3.636 |

**Step-drop, then non-monotonic plateau (minimum at 500 BCE).** 1100 BCE = 4.452 is
followed by a large immediate step down at 1000 BCE (2.172), after which PC1 runs on a
low plateau of ~0.8-2.2 that is NOT monotonic: there is a slight mid-window dip at
900 BCE (1.654, diff +2.798) and a partial rebound at 800 BCE (1.910, diff +2.542),
i.e. 800 BCE lies above 900 BCE. The lowest values are at 600 BCE (0.829) and 500 BCE
(0.815), the latter being the minimum of the window (largest difference, +3.636).
All six differences are positive; their magnitudes increase overall but not monotonically.

**What actually drops at 1000 BCE.** Deposits (ZHort) do NOT drop at 1000 BCE - ZHort is
3.38 at both 1100 and 1000 BCE, so the economic contribution to the 1100-vs-1000
difference is only +0.029; the economic gap opens only from 900 BCE (ZHort 1.73) and
becomes large from 700 BCE (ZHort -0.25). The immediate 1000 BCE step is carried by
copper-gold (ZCU_AU 2.85 -> -0.25), house size (Zhausgr 1.65 -> -0.32) and dagger
(ZDolch 1.10 -> -0.48), with monument count (ZMonument 1.352 -> -0.515) reinforcing it.
